# The live event stream is published to the stream/<session> branch only, via a
# separate git index — it must never reach main. The relay deletes its scratch
# copy at the end of a turn, but that cleanup does not run when the job is
# cancelled or hits timeout-minutes, and `git add -A` in the commit step then
# captures an empty file permanently. Ignoring the directory makes that
# impossible regardless of how the run ends (stream_push uses `git add -f`).
streams/
